The Alliance army needed light multi-purpose
exploration vehicles to gain operational independence.
The Alliance decided that light and comparatively
cheap vehicles like roofed Jeeps and Hummers were
best for this purpose. The Hummer is the name of the
civil version of the vehicle which was originally called
the Humvee in the American army. It is easy to mount
a light machine gun on its roof, its tyres are made of
a special hardened rubber, this along with a high
chassis means it can withstand very strong shocks. Its
weak point is its poor armour so it is not suitable for
direct attacks. The real advantage of the Hummer is
its mobility and speed. These features make it a very
popular vehicle.~
